  "answer": "I couldn't find an earlier ticket reporting this problem. None of the archived tickets covers Peek (PowerToys.Peek.UI.exe) being launched with an invalid runner PID argument and then staying open as a zombie process with no UI. The Peek tickets I did see are about other problems: a COM cast failure when reading File Explorer items, the wrong previewer being used for folders with a dot in the name, and previewing errors on PNG files. This looks like a new bug. As a workaround, end the PowerToys.Peek.UI.exe process in Task Manager, and avoid launching Peek directly with an arbitrary PID argument. Peek should be started through PowerToys itself, which supplies a valid runner PID."
 },
